{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening, Mr. Johnson. I'm Dr. Patel, one of the neurology doctors. You came in with nausea, vomiting, and dizziness—can you tell me more about what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. I woke up around 7:30 last night feeling really sick. I had this wave of nausea and started vomiting. At the same time, I felt like I couldn’t stand straight—like I was floating or unsteady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did you feel like the room was spinning, or was it more like you were off balance?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not spinning—just unsteady. I tried to get out of bed but had to sit back down. I also got a headache in the back of my head and neck. It was tight and pounding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any vision changes, slurred speech, or weakness in your arms or legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. I could talk fine, see clearly, and move my arms and legs. But I just felt too shaky to stand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ve given you some anti-nausea medication and fluids. Your blood sugar is high at 296, and your INR is 1.8—slightly below your target since you’re on warfarin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Coumadin for years because of my atrial fibrillation. Should I be worried about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring it closely. Right now, we’re more concerned about the dizziness and unsteadiness. Given your symptoms, we’re worried about a possible stroke in the back of the brain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A stroke? But I didn’t have weakness or slurred speech."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-11-11 00:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Strokes in the cerebellum—back of the brain—can cause dizziness, imbalance, and nausea without the classic symptoms. We’ve ordered a CT angiogram to check for blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-11-11 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. Johnson, the CT scan showed a possible issue in the left side of your cerebellum. To get a clearer picture, we’re going to do an MRI of your head."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-11-11 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it definitely a stroke?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-11-11 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We suspect it, but the MRI will confirm. The CT showed a small area with reduced blood flow in the left cerebellum, which supplies balance and coordination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The MRI is back. It confirms an acute to subacute stroke in the left cerebellum. There’s no bleeding, which is good, but we need to monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ve had a stroke? But I’m talking fine and thinking clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s in a part of the brain that controls balance, not speech or movement. That’s why you’re alert and talking well. But we saw some incoordination in your left hand during the exam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did notice my left hand was a bit clumsy. What happens now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re admitting you to the stroke service. We’ll monitor your neurological status, manage your blood pressure, and continue your warfarin carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had two strokes before. One in the right parietal lobe, another in the temporal area. Both were related to my atrial fibrillation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-11-11 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your history shows that. That’s why you’re on anticoagulants. We’ll continue warfarin for stroke prevention, but we have to be cautious with dosing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-11-12 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your INR came back at 4.2 this morning—higher than safe with a recent stroke. We’ve held your warfarin temporarily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-11-12 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? High INR?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-11-12 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It increases bleeding risk, especially with a recent stroke. We did a head CT this morning—it shows no new bleeding or swelling. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-11-12 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m okay? No bleed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-11-12 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No bleed, and no worsening of the stroke. We’ll restart warfarin at a lower dose once your INR comes down, to keep protecting you from clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-11-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve consulted neurosurgery because your stroke caused some swelling concern. They recommend close monitoring but no surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-11-12 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Surgery? I thought strokes don’t need surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-11-12 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most don’t. But large cerebellar strokes can swell and compress the brainstem. Yours isn’t large enough for that, so we’ll manage it medically."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-11-12 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-11-13 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. You stood up this morning with help and took a few steps. Your balance is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-11-13 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel a little wobbly, especially when I turn my head."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-11-13 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. The cerebellum helps with coordination. We’ve ordered outpatient physical therapy for balance and strength training."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-11-13 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been resistant to therapy before. But I’ll try this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-11-13 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. It’ll help prevent falls and improve your confidence in walking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. Your INR is back in range, and you’re walking with minimal help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my medications? Anything changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re switching you from pravastatin to atorvastatin 40 mg nightly. It’s stronger for stroke prevention. And we’re reducing your aspirin from 325 mg to 81 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why lower the aspirin? Isn’t more better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not in your case. You’re on warfarin, so high-dose aspirin increases bleeding risk without extra protection. 81 mg is safer and still effective."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. And my insulin and heart meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All staying the same. Keep checking your blood sugar. We’ll also monitor your kidney function—your labs showed some acute kidney injury, likely from dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been drinking much with all the nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-11-13 14:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Now that you’re eating and drinking, your kidneys should recover. Just keep hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today. You’re walking independently, no new neurological issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. What should I watch for after I leave?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call 911 if you have sudden vision loss, trouble speaking, weakness on one side, facial droop, or severe imbalance. These could mean another stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my weight? My cardiologist always wants me to watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—weigh yourself daily. Call your cardiologist if you gain more than 3 pounds in a day. Also, keep your neurology and primary care follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. I feel lucky this wasn’t worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re absolutely right. Catching this early and getting here quickly made a big difference. Keep up with your meds and therapy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—your diabetes is still uncontrolled. HbA1c was 7.7. Work with your doctor on tighter control to reduce future stroke risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I need to do better with my diet and insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Small steps. You’ve already taken a big one by getting care when you did. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Johnson. Stay safe and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will help you with discharge instructions and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And remember—physical therapy is key. It’ll help your balance and confidence."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll schedule it right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re on the right path."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2186-11-14 09:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-11-11 00:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-11-14 13:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with a history of atrial fibrillation on warfarin, hypertension, diabetes, hyperlipidemia, and prior strokes presented with acute onset nausea, vomiting, posterior headache, and imbalance. MRI confirmed an acute to subacute left cerebellar infarction. He was admitted to the neurology stroke service, briefly monitored in the ICU due to supratherapeutic INR and concern for swelling, but required no surgical intervention. His warfarin was held and later restarted, and aspirin was reduced to 81 mg to minimize bleeding risk. He showed clinical improvement in coordination and gait, was able to ambulate independently, and was discharged home on day four with outpatient physical therapy, medication adjustments including a switch to atorvastatin, and close follow-up for stroke prevention and diabetes management.",
    "problems": [
      "Cerebral embolism with cerebral infarction",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Chronic systolic heart failure",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified hereditary and idiopathic peripheral neuropathy",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Anticoagulants causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage I through stage IV, or unspecified",
      "Chronic kidney disease, unspecified",
      "Abnormality of gait",
      "Lack of coordination",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Body Mass Index 37.0-37.9, adult",
      "Personal history of transient ischemic attack (TIA), and cerebral infarction without residual deficits",
